Tests for the patches in patches/mutter/, run by hand.

Chromium session restore: run-chromium-session.sh and chromium_session.py
    Checks xx-session-management.patch with the client it exists for. Starts a headless mutter with one virtual
    monitor in a D-Bus session of its own and runs Chromium three times against it, through chromedriver, with a
    new profile: the first run opens three windows and quits, the second and the third restore the last session.
    Chromium speaks only the draft protocol, xx_session_manager_v1, and only with its WaylandSessionManagement
    feature, which the test enables. It covers mutter's side of the protocol, but not whether windows return to
    their workspaces, which needs a desktop. The test also runs next to your own Chromium without touching it.

    Only the mutter package has mutter's binary. Instead of installing it, extract it with its library from the
    local repository, or from any build to test:

      mkdir /tmp/mutter-root
      for p in mutter libmutter-18-0; do dpkg-deb -x /usr/local/lib/debs/${p}_*.deb /tmp/mutter-root; done
      ./run-chromium-session.sh /tmp/mutter-root /tmp/chromium-session-test

    Chromium and chromedriver default to the installed ones (packages chromium and chromium-driver), and can be
    given as third and fourth argument. With the patch, the first run sends get_session and adds its windows with
    add_toplevel. The second and the third send get_session with the session ID from the first run and restore
    the windows with restore_toplevel under the names the previous run added, each answered with restored().
    Chromium then removes each restored name and adds the window under a new one, which the next run restores:

      run 1: add_toplevel ['733961897', '733961899', '733961901']
      run 2: add_toplevel ['733961968', '733961970', '733961972']
      run 2: restore_toplevel ['733961897', '733961899', '733961901'], restored 3, removed 3
      run 3: restore_toplevel ['733961968', '733961970', '733961972'], restored 3, removed 3

    Each run also prints the size of mutter's stored sessions, which stays the same from the second run to the
    third, as the names removed and added balance. The script then prints "RESULT: OK" and exits with 0. Without
    the patch Chromium finds no xx_session_manager_v1 and sends nothing, which the summary shows as "none".

    The full WAYLAND_DEBUG output of each run is in the output directory as runN.log. The D-Bus and portal
    messages printed on the way are expected in the private session.
